{
  "area": "survival-stamina",
  "catalog": "survival-stamina",
  "description": "The stamina pool (P9c.core; catalog survival-stamina; src/stamina/stamina.ts and src/game-engine/logic/StaminaPool.ts): one meter shared by combat and traversal, spent by the action table's EnergyCost and handed to ISurvivalSystem. Ops: tuning {staminaConfig?} -> StaminaTuning (per field over DEFAULT_STAMINA_TUNING); bands {staminaConfig?, readings} -> each reading's state (exhausted if C x 100 <= M x exhaustedPercent, else winded if <= M x windedPercent, else fresh; M <= 0 is fresh); spend {current, max, cost, staminaConfig?} -> StaminaSpendResult (cost floored at 0; unaffordable moves nothing); regen {current, max, ticks, rate?, inCombat?, encumbered?, staminaConfig?} -> StaminaRegenResult (rate included) (combat rate first, then encumbered floor(base x multiplier), then base; floor(rate x ticks), capped at max); pool {staminaConfig?, costs?, actions?, actors, survivalActorId?, steps: [{do: cost (action) | afford (actor, action, cost?) | spend (actor, action, cost?) | rest (actor, ticks, inCombat?, encumbered?) | play (actor, at, inCombat?, encumbered?: the host's play clock reaches at, and the whole seconds since its last tick are rest ticks, from input start, default 0) | band (actor) | save}]} -> {tuning, steps}, a spend or rest reporting its energy/3 fact delta and host: the ISurvivalSystem calls it made (consumeStamina / recoverStamina, only for survivalActorId, only for a non-zero amount); clock {start?, tickMs?, readings} -> each reading's {now, ticks, lastTickAt} (a rest tick is 1000 ms of play, whole ticks in (lastTickAt, now], the remainder kept; none when the clock does not move or goes back). Every tick of play is rest: there is no at-rest condition beyond the rate (combat, encumbrance). Runner: src/survival/systems-corpus.ts. Every case {name, op, input, expected}; compare exactly, object key sets included; an unknown op or step is an error, never a skip. Regenerate with npm run survival-corpus; npm run survival-corpus:check fails on any difference. See docs/survival-systems.md.",
  "version": 1,
  "ops": [
    "tuning",
    "bands",
    "spend",
    "regen",
    "pool",
    "clock"
  ],
  "contract": {
    "rules": {
      "restTick": "A StaminaPool.rest tick is one second of play (STAMINA_REST_TICK_MS 1000): StaminaConfig.recoveryRate is per second, and each original template recovered recoveryRate x delta seconds. A host grants the whole seconds of its play clock since its last grant and keeps the remainder (staminaRestClock), as advanceSurvival does for the needs.",
      "atRest": "There is no at-rest condition: every tick of play recovers, including one in which the actor jumped, ran or swung (each original template recovered every frame whatever the player did). Only the rate changes: in combat the combat rate (stamina_regen/2's cut clause), encumbered the reduced rate."
    },
    "openQuestions": [
      "Whether recovery should pause for a while after a spend (a common design; none of the original engines had one): needs_ruling if wanted, with its delay."
    ]
  },
